 "evidence": "Diagnosis from existing output and offline radiation, no new runs. The box: one realization of its third lunar day (236 domain-mean outputs). The GCM: single-step heating snapshots spread evenly over the lunar day, five or six years at six sea cells, with the circulation as the remainder. The longwave codes run clear sky on lunar-day mean columns, so their heating differs from the mean of each model's own heating (nonlinearity, clouds); the sunlight copy holds water vapour alone and serves for the change between columns only. The zero-buoyancy plumes are a calculation on the box's mean sounding.",
 "reading_rule": "Every per-layer list follows PlaSim's layers top first (L0 at the top to L9 at the ground; sigma gives their full levels); bands group them (L9-L7 0-14 km, L6-L5 14-35, L4 35-48, L3 48-63, L2-L1 63-110 km at the site). W/m2 are the lunar-day mean heating of each layer's air. box.w_m2: CM1's terms laid on those layers by pressure; convection is microphysics plus resolved transport plus turbulence; forcing the mean vertical wind on the box's own air plus the day-night table; escape the curved air's extra infrared; cloud_longwave the all-sky less clear-sky longwave less the escape. gcms[run].w_m2: PlaSim's diagnostics by name, rain_evaporation the physics' sum less the listed processes, circulation the storage less the physics; convection_w_m2 is convection, large-scale condensation, rain evaporation, vertical diffusion and dry adjustment together. The radiation entries are clear sky on lunar-day mean columns: rrtmg_* CM1's RRTMG without its escape (which cm1_escape_own_column gives), plasim_clear_longwave PlaSim's with its escape unless marked without; box_column is the box's air on PlaSim's levels. adiabats: temperatures at heights_m on the box's levels, each model's air against the undiluted pseudo-adiabat of its own air near the ground, and the box's air against zero-buoyancy plumes at each eps per metre (eps_per_efolding at 270 K).",
 "producer": {
